Nice attack spells, lousy AC, bad hitpoints. Hmm - any sort of leather
armour (unless it makes you burdened) should help a bit in the AC
department; oh, and buy some protection, probably in minetown (you
have none at all right now; if you can't find convenient vaults,
identify some hard gems and sell them at jewellers and general
stores). Do Sokoban, hoping for the amulet, try to get the required
levels and then go for the quest. With, say, a -10 AC and about 100
hitpoints, it's almost trivial, and that shouldn't be too hard to
reach.

> > 2. Is it worth entering Sokoban and reverse-genociding nurses?  ie -
> > do mid-game wizards have hitpoint issues?

Hm, i really can't say. _I_ never seem to have hitpoint issues, but
i'm certainly not normal in this regard.

> Hard for me to say.  I recently ascended a wizard, but he had
> ridiculous stats (1800HP, 2000Pw), due to being somewhat extinctionist.

What do you people do on extinctionist games? Pray all the time? My
only somewhat-successful extinctionist had wiped out everything that
could be found in the dungeons apart from archons and arch-liches, and
accidentally self-genocided at 155 hp max. Well, sitting on Dlvl one
and just casting create monster all the time was _so_ *b*o*r*i*n*g*
that my brain would have liquified if i had also had to drag stuff to
altars and bother with prayer timeouts. 

> > 3. How close am I to being ready for the quest?  And what am I to
> > expect?  Any tips?
> 
> The quest is a piece of cake.  Mostly bats, and several falling rock
